{"id":17280,"name":"Trumbull County","slug":"trumbull-county","state":"Ohio","code":"OH","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/hybrid/hybrid-tax-sales-states/ohio-tax-deed-and-tax-liens/trumbull-county/","lastUpdated":"2025-05-06T02:29:15","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Foreclosure Sales","typicalSaleDate":"Thursdays, 9:00 AM","redemptionPeriod":"Starts at two-thirds of the appraised value","interestRate":"N/A","bidProcedure":"Starts at two-thirds of appraised value","deposit":"$2,000 – $10,000 depending on property value","extra":[{"label":"Auction Site","value":"Commissioner’s Hearing Room, 160 High St. NW, Warren, OH 44481"},{"label":"County Website","value":"Trumbull County Website"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed aligncenter is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"Vz9Wb5r78S4nmop\"><iframe title=\"Score Huge Discounts 40% to 90% Off Properties - Trumbull County - Ohio Tax Lien &amp; Deed Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/tv2wa0Qtylw?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Buy-Below-Market-Properties-at-Trumbull-County,-Ohio's-Tax-Foreclosure-Sales\">Buy Below-Market Properties at Trumbull County, Ohio</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Unlock a unique real estate investment opportunity through Trumbull County, <a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/hybrid/hybrid-tax-sales-states/ohio-tax-deed-and-tax-liens/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Ohio</mark></a>&#8216;s Tax Foreclosure Sales, conducted by the Sheriff&#8217;s Office. Investors can acquire properties below market prices, benefiting from lower initial investments and the potential for significant returns.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Understanding-Trumbull-County-Tax-Foreclosure-Sales\">Trumbull County Tax Foreclosure Sales</h2>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What are Tax Foreclosure Sales?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Tax foreclosure sales in Trumbull County are public auctions where properties with unpaid property taxes are sold to the highest bidder. These sales provide a way for the county to recoup unpaid taxes while offering investors a chance to purchase properties at potentially lower prices.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How They Work</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Bids start at two-thirds of the property&#8217;s appraised value. You must provide a deposit between $2,000 and $10,000, based on the property&#8217;s appraised value. If you win a bid, submit your deposit and paperwork by 2:30 PM on the day of the sale.</p>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Process if the Property Owner Does Not Redeem the Lien</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>If the property owner fails to redeem the lien, the investor may proceed to obtain a sheriff&#8217;s deed. However, access to the property is granted only after the legal confirmation of the sale.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Steps-to-Start-Investing-in-Trumbull-County-Tax-Foreclosure-Sales\">Steps to Start Investing in Trumbull County Tax Foreclosure Sales</h2>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"1\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Research and Understand Local Laws</strong> Understanding the legal framework in Trumbull County is crucial. This includes knowing the key regulations and procedures involved in tax foreclosure sales.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Visit the Local Treasurer&#8217;s Website.</strong> Check the Trumbull County Treasurer&#8217;s website for up-to-date information about tax sales. Important links include:</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.co.trumbull.oh.us/Sheriff/Services/Sheriff-Sales\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">County Tax Foreclosure Sale Information</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.co.trumbull.oh.us/sheriff\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">County Sheriff&#8217;s Office</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"3\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Check the Auction Site</strong> The Commissioner’s Hearing Room at 160 High St. NW, Warren, OH 44481, hosts Trumbull County&#8217;s tax foreclosure sales.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Read the Details about Tax Sales</strong> Make sure to read the sale schedule and other essential details available on the <a href=\"https://www.co.trumbull.oh.us/Sheriff/Services/Sheriff-Sales\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Trumbull County Sheriff&#8217;s website</mark></a>.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Contact the County Office</strong> For additional inquiries, you can contact the County Sheriff&#8217;s Office at 330.675.2508 or via email at <a href=\"mailto:sheriffsale@co.trumbull.oh.us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">sheriffsale@co.trumbull.oh.us</mark></a><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">.</mark></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Trumbull-County-Courthouse-Ohio-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-17291 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Trumbull County Courthouse Ohio\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-j